    "q-3001": {
      "dom_id": "step-q3001",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Factor the expression ${e}^{2}-18e+81.$",
      "worked_solution": "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\n{e}^{2}-2ae+{a}^{2}=(e-a)^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n{e}^{2}-18e+81.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the constant term as a perfect square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2}-18e+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2}-2\\cdot 9e+{9}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=9.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(e-9)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
